  "clean_text": "Cataract Operation Cost in india | Sankara Cataract Operation Cost in india | Sankara About Services Social Impact Donate Pledge Your Eyes Education Careers Our Blog Contact Services About Us About Pledge Your Eyes Contact Education Social Impact Services Donate Awards Dr.RVR Awards and Biography lasikblr Sankara Lasik Services OUR STORY SERVICES SOCIAL IMPACT Cataract Operation Cost in india Eyecare | 5 MIN READ July 1, 2025 Cataract Operation Cost in india Cataract Eye Operation Cost in India: What You Need to Know Cataract surgery is one of the most common and successful eye procedures performed worldwide. In India, it is not only widely accessible but also relatively affordable compared to many other countries. If you or a loved one is considering cataract surgery, understanding the Cataract eye operation cost in india is an important first step. What Is Cataract Surgery? A cataract is a clouding of the eye’s natural lens, leading to blurry vision and, if left untreated, potential blindness. Cataract surgery involves removing the cloudy lens and replacing it with a clear artificial intraocular lens ( IOL ). The procedure is typically quick—often completed in under 30 minutes—and has a high success rate Cataract Eye Operation Cost in India The cost of cataract surgery in India can vary widely based on several factors: Type of Cataract Surgery Small Incision Cataract Surgery – SICS): ₹10,000 – ₹25,000 per eye Phacoemulsification (Phaco Surgery): ₹25,000 – ₹70,000 per eye MICS Phacoemulsification (Phaco Surgery): ₹42,000 – ₹1,60,000 per eye Type of Intraocular Lens (IOL) Used Monofocal Lens Multifocal / Trifocal Lens Toric Lens (for astigmatism) Insurance & Government Support Ayushman Bharat , CGHS,ESI & State Health Schemes : Free cataract surgeries for eligible individuals Private Insurance : Most comprehensive health plans cover cataract surgery, but always check the policy terms Tips for Choosing the Right Cataract Surgery Consult an experienced ophthalmologist..."
